From 7e1f847c3f01fe34b08b8c4cf8fe1aedb7dff198 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <will-tm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:54:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/36] hw/sd: SDIO card and the card interrupt

Taken as is from the dm-lumyo QEMU tree (0008-t33-sdio): an I/O-only
sdio-card (CMD5/52/53, CCCR/FBR/CIS) whose functions live in a chip
model implementing the sdio-function interface, plus a level-sensitive
card interrupt that sdhci re-latches when Linux unmasks CARD_INT.
